+# Daily Grind
+
+Requires Node.js 22 or later. Run `npm start` to serve the homepage on port 11222
+(override with `PORT`). No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+Newsletter signups POST to `/api/newsletter` and are appended to
+`data/newsletter.jsonl` only after validation. Set `DATA_DIR` to a persistent private
+directory in production; back it up and restrict access because it contains email
+addresses. The server serves only explicitly listed public assets, never this data
+directory. This collects signups; it does not send newsletters or confirmation mail.
+
+Terminate HTTPS at your production reverse proxy and preserve the Node response
+headers. Set `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` to the exact public origin (for example,
+`https://dailygrind.example`) for strict Origin validation behind the proxy.
+
+The enforced `Connection-Allowlist` permits only the response origin and
+`https://images.unsplash.com`, with redirects and WebRTC blocked by default.
+CSP additionally limits connections and forms to this server, permits Unsplash only
+for images, authorizes the signup script using a fresh response nonce, and blocks
+workers. Browsers without Connection-Allowlist support enforce CSP but cannot
+provide the same network-layer coverage for navigation, resource hints, and WebRTC.
+The same-origin `/api/security-reports` endpoint accepts bounded reports and logs
+only receipt, never report URLs or customer data.
+
+Run `npm test` for in-process policy, endpoint, and client failure checks. The tests
+do not open a browser, listen on a port, or import the server entrypoint.
